WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.042 --> 00:00:12.882
was at the park.

2
00:00:13.603 --> 00:00:16.024
Today was her cousin's dragon boat race!

3
00:00:22.027 --> 00:00:24.989
have to meet my team now," her cousin, Peter, said.

4
00:00:25.009 --> 00:00:27.170
"The race starts soon."

5
00:00:27.190 --> 00:00:29.051
"Good luck!"

6
00:00:29.491 --> 00:00:30.212
said Grace.

7
00:00:34.924 --> 00:00:37.086
Grace and Dad walked toward the river.

8
00:00:37.106 --> 00:00:41.349
"Look!" Grace pointed to the boats on the water.

9
00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:45.872
They all had tall dragon heads and tails.

10
00:00:45.892 --> 00:00:52.456
"In China there's a dragon boat festival every spring," said Dad.

11
00:00:52.476 --> 00:00:55.859
"Why are all the boats shaped like dragons?"

12
00:00:56.519 --> 00:00:57.260
asked Grace.

13
00:00:58.641 --> 00:01:03.104
"Long ago farmers believed that dragons would bring rain," said Dad.

14
00:01:06.216 --> 00:01:08.298
"Rice needs lots of rain to grow."

15
00:01:12.141 --> 00:01:15.004
Just then Grace saw Peter with his team.

16
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:17.025
He looked worried.

17
00:01:17.045 --> 00:01:20.949
"One of our paddlers is sick," Peter said.

18
00:01:20.969 --> 00:01:23.591
"We can't race."

19
00:01:23.611 --> 00:01:28.215
"I can paddle," said Grace.

20
00:01:28.235 --> 00:01:31.557
"Thanks, Grace," Peter said.

21
00:01:31.577 --> 00:01:34.240
"But you don't know how to paddle a dragon boat."

22
00:01:35.904 --> 00:01:36.904
Grace shrugged.

23
00:01:36.924 --> 00:01:39.105
"I know how to row a canoe."

24
00:01:41.886 --> 00:01:43.686
The boat captain heard Grace.

25
00:01:43.706 --> 00:01:45.827
"Let's give her a chance.

26
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:48.167
The race starts in a few minutes!"

27
00:01:49.608 --> 00:01:51.108
"Okay," Peter said.

28
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.931
Grace jumped into the boat.

29
00:02:01.691 --> 00:02:04.632
Peter gave her a paddle and showed her what to do.

30
00:02:06.452 --> 00:02:08.954
Then a horn blew.

31
00:02:10.916 --> 00:02:12.217
The dragon boats were off!

32
00:02:14.979 --> 00:02:16.120
Boom! Boom!

33
00:02:16.821 --> 00:02:18.823
The captain stood in front with a drum.

34
00:02:21.125 --> 00:02:24.908
Each time she banged the drum, the twenty paddlers paddled.

35
00:02:27.931 --> 00:02:29.392
A boy in the back steered.

36
00:02:30.893 --> 00:02:32.134
Boom! Whoosh!

37
00:02:32.615 --> 00:02:33.836
Boom! Whoosh!

38
00:02:35.724 --> 00:02:39.787
The dragon boat flew over the water.

39
00:02:40.888 --> 00:02:42.729
The crowd roared from the shore.

40
00:02:49.494 --> 00:02:54.718
Grace cheered as their boat zipped across the finish line.

41
00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.262
place!" cried Peter.

42
00:03:00.282 --> 00:03:01.683
"Thanks, Grace.

43
00:03:02.443 --> 00:03:03.404
You saved the day!"
